"WANDERERS explains": "WANDERERS 讲解",
"Written by Claude from the measurements above. An interpretation, not a measurement.": "由 Claude 根据上面的测量结果撰写。这是解读，不是测量。",
"Barnard's Star is a small, cool red dwarf about 6 light-years away, and it moves across our sky faster than any other star. WANDERERS measured it shifting 170 arcseconds between 2010 and 2026, a speed of 10.55 arcseconds per year, within 1.5% of Gaia's 10.39. Confidence is high: all three key checks passed. The star is too bright for SPHEREx. All 242 measurements are flagged, so there is no reliable spectrum. Its brightness looked steady (−0.00 ± 0.04 mag), but that came only from the star's outer glow, so it's uncertain.": "巴纳德星是一颗小而冷的红矮星，距离我们约 6 光年，它在天空中移动得比其他任何恒星都快。WANDERERS 测得它在 2010 年到 2026 年间移动了 170 角秒，速度为每年 10.55 角秒，与 Gaia 的 10.39 相差不到 1.5%。可信度很高：三项关键检查全部通过。这颗星对 SPHEREx 来说太亮了。全部 242 次测量都被标记，所以没有可靠的光谱。它的亮度看起来很稳定（−0.00 ± 0.04 mag），但这只来自恒星的外围光晕，所以并不确定。",
