"RW Aurigae is a young star about {0} light-years away that dims unpredictably behind clouds of dust. WANDERERS found no measurable motion between {1} and {2}. Gaia lists only {3} arcseconds per year, too small to see. From September {4} to September {5} its brightness changed by +{6} ± {7} magnitudes, which is within the uncertainty, so it looked steady. A few snapshots can still miss dimming that happens between them. Confidence is medium because the star is too bright for SPHEREx, and {8} of {9} measurements are flagged as saturated.": "RW Aurigae 是一颗年轻恒星，约 {0} 光年远，会在尘埃云后面不可预测地变暗。WANDERERS 发现它在 {1} 与 {2} 之间没有可测运动。Gaia 只记录了每年 {3} 角秒，小到看不出来。从 {4} 年9月到 {5} 年9月，它的亮度变化了 +{6} ± {7} 星等，在不确定度之内，所以看起来稳定。几张快照仍可能漏掉它们之间发生的变暗。置信度为中等，因为这颗星对 SPHEREx 太亮，{9} 次测量中有 {8} 次因饱和被标记。",
