"Epsilon Indi B is a pair of brown dwarfs, objects too small to shine by fusing hydrogen, orbiting the star Epsilon Indi {0} light-years away. WANDERERS saw it move {1} arcseconds from {2} to {3}, or {4} arcseconds per year, which matches Gaia's {5}. It is {6} times brighter at {7} to {8} microns than at {9} microns, where methane in cold atmospheres absorbs light. Its brightness stayed steady within the {10} magnitude uncertainty. Confidence is high, though {11} of {12} spectrum points were flagged.": "Epsilon Indi B 是一对褐矮星（太小，无法靠氢聚变发光），环绕距离 {0} 光年的恒星 Epsilon Indi 运行。WANDERERS 看到它在 {2} 到 {3} 之间移动了 {1} 角秒，即每年 {4} 角秒，与 Gaia 的 {5} 一致。它在 {7} 到 {8} 微米比在 {9} 微米亮 {6} 倍，而冷大气中的甲烷正是在这一波段吸收光。它的亮度在 {10} 星等的不确定度内保持稳定。置信度高，不过 {12} 个光谱点中有 {11} 个被标记。",
