"R Draconis is a known red giant star about {0} light-years away. It pulsates, brightening and fading over about {1} days. Its core is too bright for SPHEREx, so all {2} spectrum measurements are flagged and we show no spectrum. WANDERERS measured the fainter edges of its image instead and found it faded by {3} ± {4} magnitudes from June {5} to June {6}. Gaia independently classifies it as this kind of variable, so confidence is high. The apparent {7}″/yr drift is below our detection limit, so it is not real motion.": "R Draconis 是一颗已知的红巨星，约 {0} 光年远。它会脉动，约每 {1} 天变亮再变暗一次。它的核心对 SPHEREx 太亮，所以全部 {2} 次光谱测量都被标记，我们不显示光谱。WANDERERS 改为测量它图像较暗的边缘，发现从 {5} 年6月到 {6} 年6月它变暗了 {3} ± {4} 星等。Gaia 独立地把它分类为这类变星，所以置信度高。表观的 {7}″/yr 漂移低于我们的探测极限，所以不是真实运动。",
